  "narrative": "The new validation evidence closes the last major open question about the four very large biomarker-dependency associations. For H6, MSI-high versus MSI-low or MSI-negative status in dependency_WRN, independent validation gives R53 = +0.821 [0.766, 0.877] at the stricter validation alpha = 0.00385, with valid cell sizes 125 and 1875. Because H6 has direction -1, this signed positive estimate corresponds to a strongly negative raw exposed-minus-comparator difference: MSI-high tumors have substantially more negative WRN dependency scores, i.e. stronger WRN dependency. This is concordant with, and slightly larger than, the discovery estimate R6 = +0.790 [0.760, 0.819]. The validated interval is very far from zero and the magnitude is far above the task's 10% clinically significant difference benchmark; relative to the observed WRN score standard deviation (~0.263), it is roughly a three-standard-deviation effect. Combined with prior internal robustness checks—Avana-library stratum R18 +0.813, batch_a main effect R41 +0.824, batch_b main effect R42 +0.789, high-mutation-burden stratum R43 +0.775, high-Cas9 stratum R44 +0.776, KRAS-wild-type context R45 +0.792, and null marker-D/E/F controls—this supports acceptance of MSI-high as a strong dataset-specific predictor of stronger WRN dependency. I close H6. This remains an association within the supplied dataset; it is not proof of causality or external generalizability. The only residual technical gap is the non-Avana WRN stratum, which could not be estimated because the exposed cell had only 10 observations in R27; however, the independent overall validation substantially mitigates the discovery-multiplicity concern.\n\nThe H17 response deadline is satisfied. KEAP1 loss versus no KEAP1 loss in dependency_NFE2L2 remains accepted: discovery R8 = +0.796 [0.776, 0.816] and validation R26 = +0.791 [0.761, 0.821]. Direction +1 means the raw exposed-minus-comparator difference is positive, so KEAP1-loss tumors have less negative NFE2L2 scores, i.e. weaker NFE2L2 dependency. This is a robust reversal of the initially hypothesized synthetic-lethal direction in H8, which remains rejected. I reaffirm H17 as accepted and closed.\n\nThe current supported large-association set is therefore: TP53 loss predicts much weaker USP7 dependency (H11 accepted and validated); KEAP1 loss predicts much weaker NFE2L2 dependency (H17 accepted and validated; H8 rejected); SMARCA4 loss predicts much stronger SMARCA2 dependency (H7 accepted and validated, with multiple stratum and specificity controls); and MSI-high predicts much stronger WRN dependency (H6 now accepted and validated). The SMARCA2 finding is further supported by Avana stratum validation H28, non-Avana discovery R28, ARID1A-wild-type stratum R35, TP53-wild-type stratum R51, and batch_a main effect R50. Role-free marker controls for these outcomes are near null, including marker-D, marker-E, and marker-F tests for WRN and SMARCA2, and marker-D for NFE2L2 and USP7.\n\nThe scientifically important negative findings remain dataset-specific and informative: direct matched oncogene-mutation or amplification associations were generally weak or null. KRAS mutation was not associated with stronger KRAS dependency; STK11 loss was not associated with KRAS dependency; BRAF V600E was not associated with BRAF dependency; ERBB2 amplification was not associated with ERBB2 dependency; TP53 loss was not associated with stronger MDM2 dependency; PIK3CA mutation was not associated with stronger STAT3 dependency; MYC amplification was not associated with stronger DHX9, RPL11, or POLR2A dependency; and BRCA2 loss was not associated with stronger KIF18A dependency. ARID1A loss overall was not associated with stronger SMARCA2 dependency, while SMARCA4 loss was strongly associated, supporting a more SMARCA4-specific paralogous dependence pattern rather than generic BAF-complex loss.\n\nEGFR amplification remains the main unresolved candidate among the clinically motivated oncogene-dependency hypotheses. Several EGFR comparisons are directionally consistent with stronger EGFR dependency, including the overall estimate R3 +0.025 [-0.000, 0.051], KRAS-wild-type context R22 +0.016 [-0.014, 0.046], TP53-loss context R37 +0.025 [-0.031, 0.080], and driver-exclusive adenocarcinoma refinement R52 +0.021 [-0.017, 0.060]. However, these point estimates are small relative to the accepted huge associations and often underpowered. EGFR should not be accepted unless a more informative stratum or pooled refinement yields a clinically meaningful, reasonably precise effect and preferably independent validation. Other unresolved questions include whether the accepted large effects persist in additional co-mutational or assay-quality strata, especially TP53-loss/USP7 and KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 in KRAS-wild-type tumors, and whether cross-outcome specificity controls such as MSI-high/POLR2A and SMARCA4-loss/POLR2A are near null.\n\nThe most informative next analyses are therefore not further validation of the already validated large associations, but (1) completing specificity controls for the large effects, especially cross-outcome controls H76 MSI-high/POLR2A and H68 SMARCA4-loss/POLR2A, plus remaining marker-E/F controls for USP7 and NFE2L2; (2) testing whether the large reversal effects remain in co-mutational contexts H69 TP53-loss/USP7 in KRAS-wild-type tumors and H70 KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 in KRAS-wild-type tumors; and (3) resolving EGFR with the registered co-mutation-stratum refinements H14, H38, H48, and related EGFR hypotheses rather than validating the weak overall EGFR signal. These analyses will better distinguish biomarker-specific associations from broader co-mutational structure, technical confounding, or underpowered small effects.",
  "research_notes": "Updated post-validation state: Four large dataset-specific associations are accepted and supported by validation in some form. H11 TP53 loss -> much weaker USP7 dependency: R11 +0.802 [0.782,0.822], validation R13 +0.800 [0.769,0.832]; accepted/closed. H17 KEAP1 loss -> much weaker NFE2L2 dependency: R8 +0.796 [0.776,0.816], validation R26 +0.791 [0.761,0.821]; accepted/closed; original H8 synthetic-lethal direction rejected. H7 SMARCA4 loss -> much stronger SMARCA2 dependency: R7 +0.784 [0.765,0.803], validation R39 +0.801 [0.771,0.830]; accepted/closed; H28 Avana stratum validated R40; H44 non-Avana R28; H36 ARID1A-wild-type R35; H67 TP53-wild-type R51; H58 batch_a main effect R50; marker-E/F/D controls null. H6 MSI-high -> much stronger WRN dependency: discovery R6 +0.790 [0.760,0.819], independent validation R53 +0.821 [0.766,0.877], alpha=0.00385, cells 125/1875; now accepted/closed. WRN supporting strata: Avana H27 R18 +0.813; batch_a H57 R41 +0.824; batch_b H63 R42 +0.789; high mutation burden H64 R43 +0.775; high Cas9 H65 R44 +0.776; KRAS-wild-type H66 R45 +0.792; marker-E/F/D null. Non-Avana WRN H43 remains invalid due exposed n=10 but independent validation reduces concern. All accepted claims remain dataset associations, not causal or externally generalizable.\n\nNegative or low-support findings: KRAS mutation vs KRAS dependency null/reject R1; STK11 loss vs KRAS R38; BRAF V600E vs BRAF R2; ERBB2 amplification vs ERBB2 R4; TP53 loss vs MDM2 R5; PIK3CA mutation vs STAT3 R12; MYC amplification vs DHX9/RPL11/POLR2A R9/R10/R24; BRCA2 loss vs KIF18A R25; ARID1A loss overall vs SMARCA2 R23 and SMARCA4-wild-type R36. These are scientifically useful matched-oncogene nulls.\n\nEGFR remains unresolved: overall R3 +0.025 [-0.000,0.051]; KRAS-wild-type R22 +0.016; TP53-loss R37 +0.025; driver-exclusive adenocarcinoma R52 +0.021 [-0.017,0.060]. Do not accept EGFR without more robust, clinically meaningful, precise stratum evidence and preferably validation. Registered unresolved EGFR refinements include H14 adenocarcinoma, H38 TP53-wildtype, H48 KRAS/TP53-wildtype.\n\nNext priorities: stop validating already validated large effects. Run specificity/context controls: H76 MSI-high/POLR2A, H68 SMARCA4-loss/POLR2A, H69 TP53-loss/USP7 in KRAS-wildtype, H70 KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 in KRAS-wildtype, H42 marker-E/USP7, H47 marker-E/NFE2L2, H74 marker-F/USP7, H75 marker-F/NFE2L2. Also run unresolved biologically motivated tests H55 STAT3/PTEN, H72 RIT1/NF1, H73 KRAS/NF1, H56 SMARCA4-loss in ARID1A-loss co-loss, and EGFR co-mutation refinements H14/H38/H48. Interpret any new large associations first with strata, marker controls, and possibly one validation if promising.",
