  "narrative": "The MDM2 clinical threshold is about 0.027 on the dependency scale using the roughly 0.27 mean score magnitude. H82, H83, H84, H85, H100, H101, and H107 all show CDKN2A-loss-associated stronger MDM2 dependency with discovery intervals entirely above both zero and the 10% threshold. The effect persists among TP53-intact and TP53-loss tumors, MTAP-intact and MTAP-loss tumors, both MTAP/TP53-intact tumors, low-9p21-copy-number tumors, and the KY library. This supports the accepted primary association (H80) as robust across several biologically and technically important strata, not merely an Avana-screen or TP53-proxy effect. The MTAP-loss CDKN2A stratum (H85) has the largest point estimate, +0.165 [0.081,0.249], while the MTAP-intact CDKN2A stratum is +0.105 [0.067,0.143]; this raises the possibility that CDKN2A loss is more strongly associated with MDM2 dependency when MTAP is also lost, but that is only a point-level contrast because the direct CDKN2A-by-MTAP interaction (H86) has not yet been tested. H99, the additional MTAP effect within CDKN2A-loss tumors, is promising but inconclusive (+0.064 [-0.025,0.153]), so I leave it unresolved and active. H101 supports that the association is present in tumors with low 9p21 copy number, but does not by itself establish broader 9p21 deletion as the causal or complete explanation. H102 shows that the huge MSI-high WRN association remains extremely strong in low-Cas9-activity screens (+0.818 [0.757,0.879]), further supporting technical robustness of H6. The new broad hypotheses are negative: MYC amplification does not show a clinically meaningful KIF18A shift, ERBB2 amplification does not show a TMED10 shift, and TP53 loss does not show an RPL11 shift. The TP53-RPL11 null is useful specificity evidence for the much larger TP53-USP7 association. I request independent validation for H85 because confirmation of the MTAP-loss CDKN2A stratum would most directly inform whether CDKN2A-MDM2 is broadly CDKN2A-associate