  "narrative": "The current supported set remains five strong dataset-specific associations: MSI-high with much stronger WRN dependency, SMARCA4 loss with much stronger SMARCA2 dependency, TP53 loss with much weaker USP7 dependency, KEAP1 loss with much weaker NFE2L2 dependency, and CDKN2A loss with stronger MDM2 dependency overall. The largest unresolved biological attribution is still whether the CDKN2A-MDM2 association is best interpreted as a broadly CDKN2A-associated MDM2 dependency phenotype, whether it is modified by MTAP co-loss, and whether it reflects broader 9p21 deletion structure. I therefore register refinements that separate deletion severity, co-deletion context, and marker-specific residual effects: CDKN2A loss in a more severe 9p21-low stratum, CDKN2A loss in a higher-copy/less-deleted stratum, MTAP loss within CDKN2A-loss and 9p21-low tumors, MTAP loss within CDKN2A-intact and 9p21-low tumors, a direct MTAP-by-low-9p21 interaction, and CDKN2A loss specifically among MTAP-loss but TP53-intact tumors. For the accepted pathway associations, I add context-robustness and specificity tests rather than new main hypotheses: TP53-USP7 and KEAP1-NFE2L2 within STK11-loss tumors, and TP53-USP7, KEAP1-NFE2L2, and SMARCA4-SMARCA2 under lower Cas9 activity. I also register STK11 loss against SMARCA2 as a specificity/negative-control test: a near-null result would support SMARCA4-specific SMARCA2 dependency rather than a broad effect of common lung co-alterations. The main directions are preserved: for direction -1, a positive signed estimate corresponds to a raw more-negative exposed dependency score; for direction +1, a positive signed estimate corresponds to a raw less-negative score. All proposed comparisons remain associations in the supplied dataset only and do not imply causality or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Core accepted dataset-specific associations remain: H6 MSI-high to much stronger WRN dependency; H7 SMARCA4 loss to much stronger SMARCA2 dependency; H11 TP53 loss to much weaker USP7 dependency; H17 KEAP1 loss to much weaker NFE2L2 dependency; H80 CDKN2A loss to stronger MDM2 dependency overall. Many accepted strata support platform/context robustness, including WRN strata, SMARCA2 Avana/non-Avana/batch/TP53-intact/CDKN2A-loss strata, KEAP1 Avana/non-Avana/CDKN2A-loss strata, and TP53-USP7 CDKN2A-loss stratum. H83 TP53-loss MDM2 stratum is accepted with validation, although validation lower bound was near the approximate 10% MDM2 threshold. Role-free marker nulls and SMARCA4 specificity nulls support outcome specificity.\n\nCDKN2A-MDM2 attribution remains the main unresolved issue. Accepted overall H80 and many strata argue the association is broad in the supplied dataset, but MTAP-loss-specific attenuation and 9p21 interaction imprecision leave attribution unsettled. Active or deferred important old claims include H85, H86, H93, H99, H109, H108, H123, and context tests H111/H112/H118/H121/H126. Newly registered proposals in this explore stage target: severe vs higher-copy 9p21 CDKN2A-MDM2 strata, MTAP effects conditional on CDKN2A and 9p21 status, a direct MTAP-by-low-9p21 interaction, CDKN2A-MDM2 within MTAP-loss/TP53-intact tumors, low-Cas9 robustness for TP53-USP7/KEAP1-NFE2L2/SMARCA4-SMARCA2, STK11-loss context for TP53-USP7/KEAP1-NFE2L2, and STK11-SMARCA2 specificity. Next analysis should prioritize these attribution/robustness tests while preserving a few broad specificity tests. Validation budget should be reserved for a genuinely new large finding or a threshold-relevant unresolved accepted claim, not for many already validated core effects. All conclusions remain associations in the supplied dataset only, not causal or externally generalizable."
