  "narrative": "The highest-value unresolved scientific question is attribution of the accepted CDKN2A-to-stronger-MDM2 association. It may reflect a CDKN2A-specific signal, MTAP co-deletion effects, broader low-copy_number_9p21 deletion structure, or a mixture. The first five proposals are targeted refinements of that attribution problem. For MDM2, the approximate absolute 10 percent clinical scale is near 0.027. For direction -1 MDM2 claims, a positive signed estimate means the exposed group has a raw more negative, i.e. stronger, dependency score. Proposal 1 asks whether the CDKN2A effect on MDM2 dependency differs by MTAP status within TP53-intact tumors with low copy_number_9p21; a positive signed interaction would indicate a stronger CDKN2A-associated raw difference in MTAP-loss tumors, whereas a negative signed interaction would indicate attenuation in MTAP-loss tumors, and a near-zero interaction would favor robustness independent of MTAP co-loss. Proposal 2 tests residual MTAP loss association when CDKN2A and TP53 are intact but low copy_number_9p21 deletion structure is present; a clinically meaningful positive signed estimate would support an MTAP or neighboring deletion contribution independent of CDKN2A loss. Proposal 3 tests MTAP co-loss within CDKN2A-loss, TP53-intact, low-copy_number_9p21 tumors, directly assessing whether MTAP status modifies the CDKN2A-loss stratum. Proposal 4 tests whether CDKN2A remains associated with stronger MDM2 dependency among low-copy_number_9p21 tumors when MTAP is intact, without restricting TP53 status. Proposal 5 tests whether CDKN2A remains associated with stronger MDM2 dependency among TP53-loss tumors when MTAP is intact. Together with the already active H153 refinement, these comparisons should help distinguish CDKN2A-specific attribution from MTAP or deletion-structure effects, though any result remains a dataset-specific association and not causal evidence. The next three proposals test whether the already accepted very large core associations also hold in KRAS-mutant lines, a clinically relevant lung adenocarcinoma context and a useful complement to the existing KRAS-wild-type robustness tests. Proposals 6 through 8 are WRN MSI, SMARCA4-loss SMARCA2, and KEAP1-loss NFE2L2 in KRAS-mutant tumors. WRN and SMARCA2 are direction -1, so positive signed estimates mean stronger dependency; NFE2L2 is direction +1, so positive signed estimates mean weaker dependency. These are expected to be large if the core associations are context robust. The final proposal is a specificity negative control: MTAP loss and USP7 dependency when CDKN2A and TP53 are intact. If null, it would support the interpretation that MTAP-related MDM2 signals, if any, are relatively MDM2-focused; if non-null, it would broaden the biological interpretation and should be followed carefully. All claims are associations in the supplied dataset only.",
  "research_notes": "Core dataset-specific accepted associations remain MSI-high stronger WRN, SMARCA4-loss stronger SMARCA2, TP53-loss weaker USP7, KEAP1-loss weaker NFE2L2, and CDKN2A-loss stronger MDM2, with several independently validated. The main active scientific uncertainty is CDKN2A-MDM2 attribution. H153 is already active and is the cleanest CDKN2A-specific stratum: CDKN2A loss among TP53-intact, low copy_number_9p21, MTAP-intact tumors. New proposals prioritize that attribution problem by adding interaction and MTAP/CDKN2A mean-difference tests within TP53-intact low-copy_number_9p21 contexts, plus CDKN2A tests when MTAP is intact in low-copy_number_9p21 and TP53-loss contexts. The KRAS-mutant WRN, SMARCA2, and NFE2L2 proposals are broad context-robustness probes; if large, they further support specificity and general context persistence within this dataset. The MTAP-USP7 test is a specificity control. If H153 or one of the new attribution tests produces a clean clinically meaningful CDKN2A-specific effect, that stratum is a preferred validation candidate. If MTAP effects are clear or interactions are clinically meaningful, validate the MTAP-specific or interaction-defining stratum instead. If all attribution tests remain imprecise, keep the question active and interpret only as entangled 9p21 deletion biology. All conclusions remain dataset-specific associations, not causality or external generalizability."
