ith much stronger SMARCA2 dependency, H7/R7 +0.784 +0.765 to +0.803 and validated R39 +0.801 +0.771 to +0.830. TP53 loss is associated with much weaker USP7 dependency, H11/R11 +0.802 +0.782 to +0.822 and validated R13 +0.800 +0.769 to +0.832. KEAP1 loss is associated with much weaker NFE2L2 dependency, H17/R8 signed +0.796 +0.776 to +0.816 and validated R26 +0.791 +0.761 to +0.821. CDKN2A loss is associated with stronger MDM2 dependency, H80/R59 +0.117 +0.082 to +0.152 and validated R66 +0.130 +0.078 to +0.182, now with validated context strata including TP53-intact low-9p21 MTAP-intact tumors, H141 and H153. Negative controls remain informative: KRAS mutation is not associated with clinically meaningful KRAS dependency, H1; BRAF V600E, EGFR amplification, and ERBB2 amplification generally lack the predicted matched-dependency signals, H2, H3, H4 and related contexts; MYC amplification is null for DHX9, RPL11, POLR2A, and KIF18A, H9, H10, H19, H110; TP53 loss is not clinically meaningful for MDM2, NFE2L2, RPL11, or STAT3 as predicted, H5, H77, H114, H151; MTAP loss alone is generally null or small, H81, H94, and H142 is near-null although not perfectly tight; BRCA2 loss is not clinically associated with KIF18A, H20; RB1 loss is not clinically associated with KIF18A, H95; PIK3CA mutation is not associated with STAT3, H12; NF1 loss is not associated with RIT1, KRAS, or STAT3, H72, H73, H96; STK11 loss is not associated with SMARCA2, H138; and role-free research markers D, E, and F are broadly null across major outcomes. The main unresolved issue is direct MTAP or deletion-structure modification of the CDKN2A-MDM2 phenotype. H153 and H157 strongly support a CDKN2A signal when MTAP is intact. Direct MTAP tests remain underpowered or near-null: H81 +0.019 -0.008 to +0.045; H94 +0.004 -0.018 to +0.026; H142 +0.009 -0.015 to +0.033; H155 +0.031 -0.028 to +0.090; H156 +0.070 -0.034 to +0.173; interactions H86, H139, and H154 are positive in some settings but intervals cross zero and the threshold. These are now deferred because the available cells are too sparse for a decisive attribution. The most informative next step is independent validation of H158, CDKN2A-MDM2 among TP53-loss, MTAP-intact, low-9p21 tumors, where discovery R134 is +0.100 +0.018 to +0.182 and the lower bound remains slightly below the threshold. If independent validation is not available, the next informative discovery analysis is H163, MTAP effect among CDKN2A-intact, TP53-intact tumors without low-9p21 deletion, together with any newly eligible large-cell MTAP strata. All conclusions are dataset-specific associations and do not establish causality or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Updated attribution synthesis. H153 is now accepted and closed because independent validation R144 +0.152 +0.061 to +0.244 confirms discovery R132 +0.113 +0.058 to +0.167 in TP53-intact, low-9p21, MTAP-intact tumors. H132 remains accepted but validation R118 +0.108 -0.024 to +0.239 is imprecise, so it is an accepted but under-confirmed MTAP-loss stratum. H93 is accepted closed as a non-Avana library stratum, +0.125 +0.029 to +0.222. Direct MTAP tests are mostly small, underpowered, or interval-wide; H154, H155, H156, H139, H140, and H143 are deferred unresolved. Core accepted associations remain WRN MSI-high, SMARCA2 SMARCA4-loss, USP7 TP53-loss weaker, NFE2L2 KEAP1-loss weaker, and MDM2 CDKN2A-loss, with multiple validations and context strata. Most informative next step: validate H158 if validation capacity is available; otherwise analyze H163 and any larger MTAP strata. Current attribution interpretation: CDKN2A-MDM2 signal appears robust when MTAP is intact, but modest MTAP or deletion-structure modification cannot be ruled out with the supplied cells."
